  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The  Accelerating the protection of women (Tipin) and girls  Rights) Project is implemented by the National Association of Women&#x2019;s Organizations in Uganda (NAWOU)in Amudat, Nakapiripirit and Moroto districts of Karamoja sub region. It is targeting 17,601 women and girls and community leaders, with the aim of preventing female genital mutilation and building the organizational capacity of 3 women rights and development organisations i.e. AIDI, KAWUO and Maendeleo Ya Wanawake.</narrative>
  </description>
